$$ ================================================================
$$ capture_regs.windbg -- x64 WinDbg / cdb command script
$$ Purpose: break immediately AFTER CreateProcessW succeeds and dump
$$          RAX RBX RCX RDX RSI RDI RSP RBP RIP.
$$ Run:
$$   cdb -c "$$><capture_regs.windbg" authorized_win64_calculator.exe
$$ or inside WinDbg: $$><capture_regs.windbg
$$ ================================================================

$$ Break on kernel32!CreateProcessW return address technique:
$$ Set breakpoint on CreateProcessW itself, then on its return frame.
bp kernel32!CreateProcessW "gu; .echo --- POST-CreateProcessW REGISTER SNAPSHOT ---; r rax,rbx,rcx,rdx,rsi,rdi,rsp,rbp,rip; .echo --- END SNAPSHOT ---; g"

$$ Alternative symbol-less breakpoint (if symbols unavailable):
$$ bp authorized_win64_calculator!main+0xNN  $$ offset of call site after CreateProcessW

$$ Start execution
g
